"Bringing more control over your connectors Mistral AI has introduced new security features related to connectors, such as enhanced admin control functions, connector-wide API keys, multi-account linkage, and debugger for safe integration with external corporate platforms. Admin controls allow you to set connector access rights for each workspace and provide detailed control over whether individual tools are activated. Introduce connector-wide API keys to prevent impersonation and support multi-account integration in automated AI workloads. Provides MCP connector debugger (public preview), connector reuse function within Vibe Code, and workflow integration function. Workflows for work that runs the business Mistral AI has released 'Workflows', an orchestration layer that helps stable production operation of enterprise AI processes, as a public preview. Workflows provide durability, observability, and fault tolerance to address failure factors in production environments, such as lack of real-time tracking of AI pipelines, network timeouts, and lack of human approval steps. Developers can write workflows in Python and publish them to Le Chat so that members of the organization can easily execute them, and every step can be audited through Studio. Various companies such as ASML, ABANCA, and France's Trabai have already adopted it and are using it to automate business processes such as global logistics document verification and KYC (Know Your Customer) review. Introducing Forge Mistral AI has launched 'Forge', a system that helps companies develop customized frontier-level AI models based on their proprietary data and knowledge. Forge allows you to build enterprise-specific models by learning internal data, such as your company's internal engineering standards, compliance policies, code base, and operational processes, instead of general public data. It supports modern training methods throughout the model life cycle, such as pre-training, post-training, and reinforcement learning, to improve workflow understanding and decision-making ability. By allowing companies to train and control models with their own datasets, they can maintain strategic autonomy while maintaining data control and intellectual property rights even in highly regulated environments. Mistral AI partners with NVIDIA to accelerate open frontier models Mistral AI participated in NVIDIA's Nemotron Coalition as a founding member to accelerate the development of open frontier artificial intelligence models and released Mistral Small 4. Mistral AI plans to participate as a founding member of the NVIDIA Nemotron Coalition and jointly develop frontier open source AI models. The two companies will collaborate by combining Mistral AI's model architecture and platform with NVIDIA's computing resources and model development tools. As part of this collaboration, we have launched the Mistral Small 4 open model to support developers, researchers, and enterprises. Leanstral: Open-Source foundation for trustworthy vibe-coding Mistral AI has released Leanstral, the first open source code agent for Lean 4 proofreading. Design an agent that can perform development and formally prove implementation to solve the human verification bottleneck. Highly sparse architecture with 6B activation parameters, optimized for realistic structured repository operation Demonstrated higher efficiency and performance than larger open source models in the FLT project's PR unit benchmark (FLTEval) OpenAI poaches Uber India’s chief to run its biggest market outside the United States OpenAI has hired former Uber India President Pravjit Singh as its first India branch manager to target the Indian market, the largest market outside the United States. OpenAI has appointed former Uber India and South Asia President Pravjit Singh as its first India MD, who will begin his term in September and report to Asia Pacific Country Manager Kiran Mani. Mr. Singh will oversee consumer growth, enterprise adoption, partnerships, government regulatory response and overall operations in the Indian market. India is OpenAI's largest market outside the U.S., with 100 million weekly active ChatGPT users, and this appointment comes as competitors such as Andropic are entering India and local AI competition is intensifying. Trustpilot just partnered with Shopify to put its reviews where AI search engines are already looking Through its partnership with Shopify, Trust Pilot strengthens exposure to AI search engines by linking reviews within shopping malls. TrustPilot has partnered with Shopify to enable Shopify sellers to display and manage TrustPilot reviews directly on their stores. During fiscal year 2025, click-through rates through AI-based search engines surged 1,490%, making it the fifth most cited domain on ChatGPT. As AI search engines and AI assistants generate recommendations based on trusted user review data, the importance of verified review data is growing. A Tokyo startup and a Beijing security firm just launched AI tools to fill the gap Anthropic’s export ban created Japan's Sakana AI and China's 360 Security have each launched alternative AI tools to fill the gap created by the U.S. Anthropic export restrictions. Tokyo's Sakana AI has released Fugu, a multi-model orchestrator with performance comparable to Fable 5. Beijing-based security company 360 Security has unveiled Tulongfeng, a vulnerability discovery tool aimed at competing with Mythos. These launches come as the U.S. government enters its third week of restrictions on exports of Anthropic's cutting-edge models. The next generation of AI won’t be powered by better models alone The core shift in AI is moving from improving model performance to building infrastructure reliability, including real-time data and browser automation. The past three years have focused on better models, but the next step will be the combination of infrastructure, systems, and real-time information surrounding models. We have passed the RAG (Search Augmented Generation) stage and are entering the Agent era, where artificial intelligence performs tasks on behalf of users. Public web data is no longer just for learning purposes, but is turning into an infrastructure problem that is utilized in real time at AI runtime (point of execution). FTC clears Musk to acquire SpaceX alumni startup Mesh, the optical hardware company his data centers need The U.S. Federal Trade Commission (FTC) approved Elon Musk's acquisition of Mesh Optical Technologies, an optical hardware startup for AI data centers. The FTC quickly cleared the antitrust review for the acquisition of Mesh Optical Technologies, a startup founded by former SpaceX engineers. Mesh Optical has optical transceiver technology (flagship product Alpha C1 transmits more than 1 terabit per second) for high-speed data transmission and reduced power consumption between servers and GPUs in data centers. Through this acquisition, SpaceX will be able to secure its own technology in the optical transceiver field, overcome the limitations of externally leased data center infrastructure, and strengthen its independent AI data center capabilities in the future. Asian AI startups launch Mythos-like  models as Anthropic’s export ban drags on Amid the US Anthropic model export restrictions, Asian startups such as China's 360 and Japan's Sakana AI are releasing corresponding AI models. Chinese security company 360 has unveiled 'Tulongfeng', an AI tool that could compete with Anthropic's Mythos. Japan's Sakana AI has launched 'Fugu', an AI model for agents that rivals Anthropic's Fable 5 and Mythos Preview and can orchestrate other models via API. The move comes two weeks after the U.S. government imposed global export restrictions on Anthropic's powerful models for security reasons. Trump Admin releases Anthropic  Mythos to be used by more than 100 US companies, agencies Two weeks after the ban, the U.S. Trump administration allowed Antropic's powerful cybersecurity AI model, 'Mythos 5', to be provided again to more than 100 U.S. organizations and companies. The Trump administration has relaxed its stance to allow access to the Mythos 5 model to major U.S. organizations and corporations, as well as non-U.S. employees of those organizations and Antropic. Commerce Secretary Howard Rutnick said he had determined appropriate safeguards were in place and granted access only to trusted partners. Cybersecurity models Mythos 5 and Fable 5 were withdrawn from the market after their safeguards were easily bypassed by security researchers, a move that excludes the relaunch of Fable 5. Why is Apple asking me to pay more for Big Tech’s AI obsession? Analysis shows that the rise in component prices due to AI competition among big tech companies is ultimately leading to increases in device purchase prices for consumers. Big tech companies, including Apple, are raising the prices of consumer devices such as MacBooks and iPads due to the surge in RAM prices due to the concentration of HBM memory production for AI data centers. RAM and storage supply shortages and prices continue to rise as component manufacturers prefer to produce more profitable AI server chips instead of consumer DDR5 Apple has passed on component cost increases to consumers despite posting record earnings in recent quarters and maintaining margins above the industry average. Anthropic&#8217;s Mythos 5 is back The US Trump administration has approved limited redistribution of Enthropic's powerful cybersecurity AI model, Mythos 5, but the release of Fable 5 for the public remains uncertain. License requirements have been revised as Enthropic works with the U.S. government to address model-related risks. Access to the Mythos 5 model has been limited to a limited number of trusted cyber defenders and infrastructure providers. This exemption allows non-US Enthropic employees and members of approved organizations to access Mythos 5. Building Supervised Fine-Tuning Data from NVIDIA Open-SWE-Traces: Trajectory Parsing, Patch Analysis, Token Budgets, and Tool-Use Metrics This is a tutorial on how to use NVIDIA's Open-SWE-Traces dataset to analyze agent software engineering trajectories and build data for map refinement (SFT). By streaming the Open-SWE-Traces dataset directly from Hugging Face, data analysis and preprocessing are performed efficiently in the Google Colab environment. After normalizing the multi-party conversation, parsing the final code patch, and extracting metadata, an analysis data frame such as trajectory length, tool usage, and success is created. Curate high-quality SFT subsets based on success labels, token limit (MAX_SFT_TOKENS = 32000), programming language filters, etc. Detecting and Controlling Sycophancy with Cascading Linear Features We propose a new data generation pipeline and interpretation framework that separates cascading linear features to detect and control user sycophancy phenomenon. Step-by-step samples that scale linearly beyond simple binary control sample pairs effectively isolate features responsible for behavior. The discovered flattery features form a linearly separable subspace, allowing us to detect and control model activation more accurately than existing methods. The proposed method has similar or better performance compared to LLM-as-a-judge or system prompting approaches while providing lower computational cost and interpretability guarantees. Refusal Lives Downstream of Persona in Chat Models This paper studies the interaction between the rejection phenomenon and persona characteristics in the Large Language Model (LLM) and demonstrates that rejection responses can be suppressed through obedient persona adjustment. The intervention was conducted by extracting the obedient persona direction and rejection direction from the Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct and Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct models. Steering toward an obedient persona significantly suppressed the rejection response, with the Llama model's rejection rate plummeting from 97% to 2%. Since the rejection phenomenon is gated at a later layer representation stage downstream of the persona direction, treating rejection as a single isolated direction overlooks its dependence on the persona. AlgoEvolve: LLM-driven Meta-evolution of Algorithmic Trading Programs We propose AlgoEvolve, an evolutionary framework that leverages Large Language Models (LLM) to automatically generate and improve algorithmic trading programs that can adapt to complex and ever-changing financial markets. We present AlgoEvolve, a framework that leverages LLM as a mutation operator in evolutionary algorithms to generate, evaluate, and iteratively improve trading strategies expressed in Python code. We demonstrated through experiments that the system adapts to changes in market conditions and autonomously changes trading rules, resulting in adaptive strategy logic. By introducing a meta-evolution loop that evolves the prompt itself that drives program synthesis, we find search heuristics that outperform initial human-designed instructions and reduce failure cases where no transaction occurs at all. Agentic Analysis for Agentic Infrastructure: An LLM-Powered Pipeline for Comparative Governance of DAO and Corporate AI Protocols In order to comparatively analyze the governance structure of AI agent protocols on a large scale, this study introduced an LLM-based pipeline and applied it to an on-chain method and a company-led method. We compared and analyzed governance discourse using the AI ​​agent interoperability standard ERC-8004 (permissionless on-chain) and Google A2A (corporate-led) as a control group. Analysis of 4,323 governance participation records showed that both methods showed similar levels of participation inequality and community fragmentation. In a permissionless (on-chain) environment, the alignment of discourse appears more dense, suggesting that open governance can promote greater thematic convergence even amid decentralized participation. Accelerating Skill Assessment in Chess: A Drift-Diffusion-Enhanced Elo Rating System Leveraging the Drift Diffusion Model (DDM) from cognitive neuroscience in competitive chess, we propose DD-Elo, a rapid chess skill evaluation system that reflects not only the player's match results but also each move-step decision. Because the existing Elo Rating system is based only on game results, there is a time lag in reflecting changes in skill. The proposed DD-Elo system models skill expression as a decision-making process, integrating data from purchase stages and capturing rapid skill fluctuations. Through mathematical proof, it was confirmed that DD-Elo maintains the deviation from the existing Elo system within a certain range, and its ability to adapt to skill changes more quickly was demonstrated through experiments. US allows Anthropic's Mythos AI to be released to 'trusted' US organizations The US government has unblocked Antropic's powerful AI model 'Claude Mythos 5' and allowed its disclosure to trusted US institutions and companies. The U.S. Department of Commerce has lifted the block on Antropic's Claude Mythos 5 model for more than 100 places, including certain trusted partners and government agencies. This action is the result of close daily consultations between Antropic and the U.S. government to establish safeguards with the goal of securing national security and AI leadership. However, the weakened version, Fable 5, is excluded from this approval, and the timing of access for non-US governments and general consumers is still unclear. Anatomy of an attack believed to be behind a failed state Analysis of a backdoor attack technique that plants malicious code in the developer's TypeScript project execution path and spreads PinpinRAT under the guise of a fake venture capital (VC) interview. The attacker approached Lua Ventures as a fake person, gained trust through email and Google Meet calls, and then led them to launch a Ticket Harbor repository disguised as a recruiting assignment. Implements a malicious stub to automatically run when TypeScript is executed through the patch-package and typescript+5.9.2.patch files in the repository, and uses git skip-worktree to hide the malicious patch in git status. The executed stub passes through the hidden chunk behind the image file (operators/3.png) and the WASM stub to run the 1.68MB PinpinRAT payload as a separate process to perform host information collection, file upload/download, and self-removal. Automation of detailed planning workflow completed with &#039;planning harness&#039; This is about the construction and use of 'Planning Harness', a system that controls AI to automatically create detailed plans under consistent rules and context. By setting the rule file (CLAUDE.md) in a local folder, we solved the problem of manual detailed planning by introducing the planning harness concept that forces AI to recognize and operate planning rules at all times. Unlike one-time prompting, planning harness has a pipeline that is always on standby, and AI can directly modify local files with File I/O permission and share them with team members through GitHub. When the comment function is added, sequence diagrams, user flow charts, and HTML distribution are automatically created with just a single line request, and it is expected to expand to wireframe automation in the future by integrating visual tools such as Figma MCP. Akrites open letter to protect open source security together In response to the acceleration of AI-based vulnerability discovery, 'Akrites', a collaboration involving global IT companies, has been launched to jointly supplement and coordinate core open source software security. As AI models can discover multiple vulnerabilities in a matter of minutes, the response burden on existing open source maintainers has increased dramatically. Major IT companies and organizations, including AWS, Google, Microsoft, and OpenAI, are participating to provide confidential coordination points, dedicated security incident response teams, and support upstream remediation. As reverse engineering attacks using AI have become faster after the release of patches, the success criterion is the actual system deployment rather than the simple release of the patch. US government to decide who will use GPT-5.6 The U.S. Trump administration is expanding its policy of directly screening and regulating companies that have access to OpenAI and Anthropic's latest AI technologies, citing security concerns. The Trump administration sharply changed its regulatory stance due to concerns about AI's ability to discover software security vulnerabilities. OpenAI has restricted access to its latest model, Sol, to only companies approved by the U.S. government. The Department of Commerce sent a letter to Anthropic allowing it to offer the Mythos 5 model only to its trusted partner list, which includes about 100 companies. Showcase: Building ML models that \"watch\" MMA fights and label events and positional changes making these moments all searchable on a timeline [P] This article is about developing an ML model that analyzes MMA fight videos to detect position changes and key events and make them searchable in a timeline. The developer, a former amateur MMA fighter and BJJ brown belt, developed the cagesight.ai service by incorporating ML/AI technology. This ML model 'watches' the game video, detecting positions such as standing, clinch, and ground, as well as key events such as knockdown and takedown. The timeline marker created at the bottom of the game provides users with the ability to jump directly to the desired game moment. Kicking off GPU Mode [D] The first installment of a series documenting work on GPU infrastructure, LLM, computer vision, and CUDA kernel optimization is here. We cover why GPUs have become the industry's mainstay, the difference between CPU/GPU, and the importance of nvidia-smi. We plan to address empirical differences in GPU architectures across generations, including Ampere, Hopper, and Blackwell, in the future. We plan to analyze the asynchronous memory paradigm using TMA/wgmma and solving register pressure for kernel optimization. What does it mean to be a mathematician when AI does the math? Discussion and reflection on the impact of advances in AI technology on mathematicians' research motivation, research methods, and the future of the field of mathematics Mathematicians find beauty and deep satisfaction in studying complex mathematical problems in depth and finally reaching understanding. Professor Terence Tao predicts the advent of the era of 'Big Mathematics', in which humans and artificial intelligence collaborate to solve complex problems. Although some applied mathematics research can be completed quickly with computer calculations and AI support, the abstract problem-solving process and logical reasoning process of pure mathematicians have human significance beyond mere speed. Best Buy's gaming deals are still live after Prime Day - Nintendo Switch, PS5, and more There is news that Best Buy is continuing to offer discounts on games and PC hardware even after Amazon Prime Day ends. Amazon Prime Day is over, but Best Buy's Tech Fest sale runs until Sunday. The discount includes a wide range of gaming devices and hardware, including mice, keyboards, high-performance laptops, console gaming devices, as well as DDR5 RAM kits. High-performance CPUs and high refresh rate (240Hz) LG UltraGear OLED 45-inch curved monitors suitable for content creation and competitive games were introduced as major discount products. Sony is still selling last year's flagship OLED TV for $600 off - and I highly recommend it Here's the news that Sony's OLED TV, the Bravia 8 II model, is on sale at a discount, as well as detailed reviews and recommendations. The Sony Bravia 8 II 65-inch model is on sale for a discount of $600 and the 55-inch model for $300, but it is still expensive at over $2,200. The screen brightness is dimmer than LG or Samsung's OLED TVs, but it has the advantage of allowing you to fine-tune the screen and audio settings. Acoustic Surface Audio+ technology, which uses the screen itself as a speaker, and Dolby Atmos support provide immersive sound, and the mode switches automatically when PS5 is connected. Some of the best Amazon Prime Day SSD and storage deals are still live - Samsung, WD, and more We introduce information on SSD and storage discounts from major brands such as Samsung, WD, and Seagate that are still ongoing even after Amazon Prime Day ends. Even though the Amazon Prime Day sale has ended, you can purchase M.2 and external SSD products from major brands such as Samsung, WD, and Seagate at significant discounts. Key products introduced include a 1TB portable SSD supporting 256-bit AES encryption, a 2TB professional SSD with an improved heatsink (supporting Samsung Magician), and the Seagate 1TB portable SSD with USB-C connectivity and data recovery services. This is a great opportunity for consumers who have been thinking about upgrading their workstation or gaming PC to expand storage according to their budget and usage. 13 Google Photos settings I always change on every new device - and why When starting Google Photos on a new device, here are 13 recommended settings you should adjust first to protect your privacy and manage storage capacity. You must make sure that your Google Photos backup account is set to your main Google account, not a work or secondary account. Instead of backing up all your photos and videos, we recommend that you select only specific device folders for backup by setting limited access permissions. Backing up all screenshots and downloaded files to the cloud will waste storage space, so you should review your backup settings in advance. This mesh system will make your at-home Wi-Fi lightning fast - and it's still 30% off for Prime Day TP-Link's high-speed Deco 7 Pro mesh WiFi system is on sale for Amazon Prime Day. The TP-Link Deco 7 Pro 3-pack is on sale for $500, a 29% discount during Amazon Prime Day. The Deco 7 Pro 3-pack covers up to 8,100 square feet and supports connectivity for over 200 devices. It is equipped with an AI-based function that automatically switches the device to the node with the strongest connection signal depending on the travel route. OpenAI Previews GPT-5.6 Sol With Restricted Access and Stronger Cyber Safeguards OpenAI has released preview versions of GPT-5.6 Sol, Terra, and Luna with enhanced cybersecurity measures and strict access restrictions. As part of its collaboration with the U.S. government, OpenAI has released three versions of GPT-5.6 (Sol, Terra, and Luna) with stronger safeguards in limited preview to select companies. GPT-5.6 Sol has the best performance ever in the cybersecurity field, demonstrating competitive performance with only one-third of the output tokens compared to Anthropic Mythos Preview based on ExploitBench. Although the model excels at detecting vulnerabilities and developing exploits, it cannot perform autonomous end-to-end attacks, and agent coding tasks are more prone to deviating from user intent than previous versions. ‘Missos 5’ limited distribution allowed in the US… 'Fable 5' remains banned While the U.S. government approved limited distribution of Antropic's cutting-edge AI model 'Missos 5' only to a few trusted organizations in the US, it maintained a ban on 'Fable 5', raising controversy over government market control and fairness. The U.S. Department of Commerce allowed 'Misos 5', which had been ordered deactivated due to security risks, to be redeployed to over 100 trusted organizations, including companies participating in 'Project Glasswing', within two weeks. Institutions and employees (including foreigners) selected through this permit can use it without a separate license, but regulations for 'Fable 5' for the general public, general companies, and overseas are maintained. Since the government arbitrarily selected approval targets without clear standards, the AI ​​industry, civic groups, and OpenAI CEO Sam Altman are criticizing it for lack of transparency and market distortion. Baidu unveils ‘Unlimited OCR’… “Break memory limits and document dozens of pages at once” Baidu has released 'Unlimited OCR', an open source OCR model that can process dozens of pages of documents at once by solving the problems of increased memory usage and slow speed. By introducing the reference sliding window attention (R-SWA) structure, KV cache size and memory usage are kept constant even when processing long documents. Developed based on Deep Seek OCR, it applies an MoE structure that activates only 500 million out of 3 billion parameters during inference and a 16x token compression technology. It recorded the highest performance in the OmniDogBench benchmark and maintains up to 35% higher performance than the existing model with a processing speed of 5580 tokens per second. Agent long-term project benchmark 'AA-Briefcase' revealed... 1st place is 'Fable 5' A new benchmark 'AA-Briefcase', which evaluates how well an AI model performs a long-term corporate project lasting several weeks, has been released. It is a long-term project-based benchmark that breaks away from the existing single question answer method and requires analysis of large-scale, contradictory and incomplete data like a real business environment. As a result of the first evaluation, 'Claude Fable 5' ranked first, but was the most expensive, and open source models such as Zipu AI's 'GLM-5.2(max)' showed excellent cost-effectiveness. Even the highest performance model has a standard completion rate of only 3%, and performance deteriorates as the number of reference documents increases, confirming the long-term task performance limitations of current AI technology. Nvidia unveils ‘GLM-5.2’ 4-bit quantization model… “Maintains accuracy and capacity ↓ 70%” NVIDIA has released Zipu AI's large language model 'GLM-5.2' by optimizing it with its own 4-bit quantization model that reduces capacity by about 70% without loss of accuracy. NVIDIA has released the checkpoint optimized for GLM-5.2, a 753 billion parameter scale MoE model, through NVFP4 quantization technology to Hugging Face. Reduces GPU memory usage by significantly compressing the 1.5TB capacity of the existing FP8-based original model to 410GB without reducing performance. As a result of the benchmark, performance similar to the original was maintained, but in workloads where the actual decoding speed is a bottleneck, the single stream processing speed may decrease due to non-support for speculative decoding. Deepseek's attraction of external investment is due to the 'Misos shock'... \"We can't survive with only high efficiency\" The story is that Deepseek, shocked by the overwhelming infrastructure-based performance shown by Antropic's 'Missource', revised its high-efficiency strategy and began to attract large-scale external investment to expand computing and invest in infrastructure. After witnessing Antropic Mysos' autonomous performance and large-scale infrastructure results, Deepseek CEO Wenpeng Liang decided that it would be difficult to survive in the frontier AI competition without massive capital, so he attracted investment. The secured investment of $7.4 billion will be used to expand computing, and Deepseek plans to strengthen its 'harness team' to develop autonomous AI agents and increase the workforce in all departments by at least two times. CEO Liang is sticking to the existing strategy of achieving AGI through open source while adopting the American-style large-scale capital investment model, and sees coding tools as nothing more than temporary products. ‘Computer Use’ built into Gemini 3.5 Flash… Screen operation, search, and map all at once Google has built in the 'Computer Use' function as a basic tool in Gemini 3.5 Flash, allowing screen manipulation, search, and map linking to be handled inexpensively in a single model. On June 25th, local time, Google integrated the 'Computer Use' function, which operates software like a mouse and keyboard, into Gemini 3.5 Flash as a native tool. In the OSWorld-Verified benchmark, Gemini 3.5 Flash scored 78.4 points, showing performance close to the high-performance model GPT-5.5 (78.7 points). The price is $1.50 for input and $9 for output per 1 million tokens, which is one-third of GPT-5.5, which can lower the agent introduction cost. OpenAI, GPT-5.6 released... Limited distribution upon U.S. government request OpenAI has unveiled the next-generation AI model 'GPT-5.6' series, but at the request of the US government, limited distribution to trusted partners will be carried out first. OpenAI launched the GPT-5.6 series (Sol, Terra, Luna) with improved performance, and Terra lowered the price by half compared to its predecessor. The 'Maximum Inference Effort' option, which gives more inference time to the model, and the 'Ultra Mode' new feature, which uses sub-agents for parallel processing, were introduced. Due to the sharing of prior plans with the U.S. government and the impact of the executive order, we will begin with limited disclosure to trusted partners instead of immediate general distribution."